As for pools, it seems that water in general needs an expanded treatment.
Pools could have their own set of effects just as fountains do now.  Right
now they are just a space to avoid and a nuisance, adding very little
value to the game.  Having to deal with pools/water in a more interactive/
strategical way would enhance the game further and alleviate the "sudden
death" phenomenon for pools that most people seem to dislike.  Several
people have already made suggestions about pools.  In particular I like
the multi-spaced pools (read: ocean/sea/lake); perhaps a unique level with
most of the level filled with water.  This would lead to a greater variety
of water creatures, and boats, and swamps, and iced-over lakes...

